    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_ab720a16",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image features a man in a suit with arms outstretched, overlaid with text that reads: 'everyone talking about protecting minority rights needs to remember there is no smaller minority than the individual.' The scene is a rhetorical or philosophical statement, using the man's expressive gesture to emphasize the message. The overall intent is to provoke thought about the concept of individual rights within the context of minority rights discourse. The meme does not contain any explicit abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, hateful, misogynous, or propaganda elements. The message is philosophical and intended to highlight the individual as the smallest possible minority, thereby underscoring the importance of protecting individual rights as a foundational principle. The intent is to use the visual of a speaker to reinforce the textual message through analogical mapping: the speaker's open, inclusive gesture visually mirrors the idea that every individual is a unique and irreplaceable minority.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_5d7a6619"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_b2e966b7",
